  {
    "episode_id": 74039,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74039.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Great to have you along for the ride. Thanks a lot for stopping by. Glad to have this guy on. He is the District 6 Republican, great state of Virginia Congressman Ben Klein. Ben, how are you? Good to see you. Joe, great to be with you. Thanks. I'm really glad to have you. So I want to jump right into the state of the union address, if you don't mind, where the president went on and on about how great the economy is. And thankfully, he was called out by some Republicans during the speech. I thought it went overboard a bit because protocol does matter. But there were so many lies and so many half-truths and so many just imaginary things that he was talking about. You almost had to call him on the carpet because you guys basically don't have any access to Biden, do you?",
