  {
    "episode_id": 74039,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74039.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Exactly. And as we negotiate the debt ceiling increase, we need ways to bring our budget into balance, our fiscal responsibility back. And as we, but we're not going to touch Social Security and Medicare, and as we work toward a balanced budget on the Budget Committee, and we're going to make sure that we balance in 10 years, but we do it in a way that strengthens Social Security and Medicare. You know, right now they're due to go and solve it in 10 years. The interest on the debt from all of this radical democrat spending over the last four years is crowding out other non-discretionary spending. It's about the size of health care and veterans and defense all combined. So interest on the debt is overwhelming us and we've got to get our handle on it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
