    "turn_text": "It is Congressman Ben Klein, District 6 Republican, great state of Virginia. He's also in the House Freedom Caucus, which is a big deal because you guys had a very big voice in the election of a Speaker of the House, and I'm glad that you got some provisions that you wanted, which was awesome. You're also a member of this new subcommittee on responsiveness and accountability to oversight. It's not that long ago that Donald Trump, when he was the president, would walk out. A gag of reporters would be there. He'd give him 15, 20, 30 minutes. Then COVID every day, he was going to have a 15 minute news conference. He stood there for two hours and argued with Jim Acosta. We have no access to Biden whatsoever. We're hearing from KJP, Karine Jean-Pierre. I'm not sure she ever even talks to him, but she doesn't say anything. Just a bunch of revolving answers to questions that she's not really answering, and she says I answered them already. So we get nothing from this administration. Are you going to be able to in the house? hold their feet to the fire and get some oversight into why the Department of Transportation is so bad. Why Jennifer Granholm doesn't know anything about energy, yet she's speaking about energy. Why Biden says he cut the deficit by $1.7 trillion when he clearly didn't. He actually just lowered it from the overwhelmingly high deficit he had the year before. So when we get some real oversight, because the American people are getting a little bit sick and tired of the lack of transparency as they tell us they're being transparent.",
