    "turn_text": "Absolutely. He needs to go. But what we're going to do, I'm proud to be a member of the Freedom Caucus, and I'm so proud of Jim Jordan as chair of Judiciary, leading the charge. I'm going to the border with him here soon. He's going to be pushing hard to make sure we have that oversight over the Department of Justice as chair of the select committee on the weaponization of our intelligence agencies, making sure that we hold those accountable who went after conservatives and media conservatives and Twitter and online conservatives, just average constituents who are expressing their conservative views online. But to be named by the chairman of the subcommittee on responsiveness and accountability to oversight is an honor and I look forward to working to make sure that that's another tool in toolbox. So as they go to DOJ and as they say we want these documents, we want this testimony, we want to make sure that we get the information that the people deserve, that I'm there to drag them up to the hill, to hold them accountable, to be that bulldog for the oversight process. And they put Eric's wall as my ranking member. They're taking it seriously. They know that this is another tool that can be effective. And so we're looking forward to using it and to holding those entities accountable as we conduct our oversight.",
