    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74039.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "I'm glad that you're chairing the subcommittee. It is Ben Klein, U.S. Representative, great state of Virginia, go to client.house.gov. Let's talk about Alejandro Mayorkas. We've got over 5 million illegals coming across the border in just two years. That doesn't count for those who we didn't even see. Those are just the ones that we got. under Trump, we had 60, 70-year historic lows in illegal crossings. He just followed the law as it is. He followed the law and actually told CBP, the Border Patrol, to go ahead and enforce it. My work is clearly not making them enforce it. We're giving everybody parole. We're acting like everybody gets an asylum claim when we know 90%. Don't qualify for asylum now. We got non-governmental organizations, NGOs in Mexico actually doing the paperwork for these people before they ever hit the border. So Biden and his administration aren't even counting those people as illegal crossings. Then something's got to stop here. I mean, something's got to happen. Can you get rid of my orcas? Can you impeach him? I don't know that the Senate would agree, but can you at least force him to resign and put somebody else in place? And is it really him or is it the policies he's told to follow that are the problem? Is it him or the policies?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
